# Cloudflare Pages header rules.
#
# Consumed at build time and never served as a file. Only paths that need to
# differ from the platform default (public, max-age=14400, must-revalidate)
# belong here.

# The What's New content constant is the one file in the build that changes on
# its own schedule — a new issue is published by editing it and pushing, with
# no code change anywhere else (PRD §5.11.13). Under the default four-hour
# max-age a browser will not even ask the server during that window, so a
# freshly published issue stays invisible to anyone who visited recently,
# including whoever is checking the publish worked. That happened on the first
# real publish, 2026-08-03.
#
# no-cache does not mean "do not store" — the browser still caches, it just
# revalidates first. The file is ~2KB with a strong ETag, so a revalidation is
# a 304 with no body. Cheap, and it keeps publishing to "edit the constant,
# push" with no cache-bust step to forget.
/_lib/whats-new-data.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
